thread:
marta: heads up — ran into import errors when upgrading to 0.7.1 of the node SDK in a Next app that uses both serverless and edge functions. stack trace shows ESM/CJS mismatch and sourcemaps all point to transpiled code. anyone else?

alex: yep saw that yesterday on a customer app. root cause was our published package changed to only ship ESM entrypoints but some tooling (vite SSR + older consume patterns) still resolves require paths. also sourcemaps were stripped in the cjs build.

jin: quick Q — are you using the SDK directly in edge runtime (Edge API Routes / middleware) or only in server code? behavior differs.

marta: primarily edge middleware and a serverless API fallback. bundle size and streaming are also behaving differently on edge — streaming responses fail with "ReadableStream is not a constructor" in Vercel Edge.

sam: streaming issue is the classic runtime mismatch. Cloudflare/Vercel expect web streams; node-streams/polyfill mismatch can break. we should document that the edge build must import the ESM bundle that uses web streams, not the CJS/stream polyfilled one.

alex: proposed short-term mitigation: publish a dual-entry bundle and add explicit package.json exports so bundlers pick correct target. example exports layout we've tested locally: ```json
"exports": {
  ".": {
    "import": "./dist/esm/index.js",
    "require": "./dist/cjs/index.cjs",
    "default": "./dist/esm/index.js"
  },
  "./stream": {
    "import": "./dist/esm/stream.js",
    "require": "./dist/cjs/stream.cjs"
  }
}```

jin: also add "type": "module" at package root only if shipping ESM-first; but that breaks require resolution for some older bundlers. safer to keep package type unspecified and rely on exports conditions.

marta: thanks — what about sourcemaps? Next/Vite show original TS files in dev but production sourcemap files point to bundled code.

sam: we accidentally omitted sourceMappingURL for cjs artifacts during rollup. fix: ensure rollup outputs include sourcemap: true and that we emit .map files next to both esm and cjs artifacts. also ensure package.json points "types": "dist/index.d.ts" so TS tooling can pick correct maps.

alex: for edge runtime docs, note these quick checklist items: 1) import the ESM entrypoint (use "import" condition in exports); 2) ensure your app's bundler is configured to leave web streams alone (Vite: optimizeDeps.exclude + ssr.noExternal for the SDK); 3) don't polyfill node streams in edge bundles; 4) prefer fetch-based auth for edge (avoid node-only http libs).

jin: pinging @build-bot — can you run a quick CI build matrix for node 16/18 (+ vite & next) with the dual-export patch and publish a rc tag?

build-bot: CI triggered for branches: feature/dual-exports. Running matrix: node16-vite, node18-vite, node18-next-edge. ETA ~12m.

marta: copying the snippet I used to force Vite to keep SDK ESM in ssr build: ```js
// vite.config.js
export default {
  ssr: {
    noExternal: ['@redwood/inference-sdk']
  },
  optimizeDeps: {
    exclude: ['@redwood/inference-sdk']
  }
}
```

sam: good pattern. for next.js edge middleware also add `transpilePackages: ['@redwood/inference-sdk']` in next.config.js if using app dir.

marta: PR up at https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/482 — it's the dual-entry + sourcemap fix. can someone review the packaging bits? small change to rollup config and package.exports.

alex: I'll review now — leaving a couple inline comments on CJS sourcemap paths.

jin: FYI I hit a small retry behavior quirk in edge: our retry wrapper used setTimeout which is not available in certain edge runtimes; replaced with a micro-delay via async/await + Promise.resolve loop and it fixed it. share patch in the PR.

marta: awesome. once CI green we can cut rc and add a short note in the SDK README about edge usage and the Vite/Next config snippets.

sam: slight follow-up — add an automated test that builds with vite+ssr and asserts the bundle uses the esm/stream file (cheap smoke test). I'll open a follow-up. :thumbsup:

marta: thanks team, will sync if CI flags anything. :sparkles:
